> 
> # 3. `test_multi_user_memory_is_isolated`
> 
> ## Purpose
> Verify that memory for one user is not retrieved for another user.
> 
> This is absolutely essential once you support multiple users.
> 
> ## Why it matters
> Cross-user leakage is one of the worst possible bugs in a memory system.
> 
> ## Test setup
> Use two users:
> - `alice`: memory about Python
> - `charlie`: memory about gardening
> 
> Search from each account and ensure only own memories are returned.
> 
> ## Example test
> 
> ```python
> def test_multi_user_memory_is_isolated():
>     store = InMemoryStore()
>     model = MockMemoryModel()
>     index = SimpleTextMemoryIndex(store)
>     ltm = LongTermMemory(store=store, model=model, index=index)
> 
>     ltm.remember(
>         MemoryRecord(
>             memory_id="",
>             user_id="alice",
>             kind="fact",
>             content="Alice uses Python for AI",
>             summary="Alice uses Python for AI",
>             created_at=datetime.utcnow(),
>             source="test",
>             importance=0.9,
>             confidence=1.0,
>             tags=["python"],
>         )
>     )
> 
>     ltm.remember(
>         MemoryRecord(
>             memory_id="",
>             user_id="charlie",
>             kind="fact",
>             content="Charlie grows tomatoes",
>             summary="Charlie grows tomatoes",
>             created_at=datetime.utcnow(),
>             source="test",
>             importance=0.9,
>             confidence=1.0,
>             tags=["gardening"],
>         )
>     )
> 
>     alice_results = ltm.retrieve_by_keywords("alice", query="Python", limit=10)
>     charlie_results = ltm.retrieve_by_keywords("charlie", query="Python", limit=10)
> 
>     assert any("Python" in m.content for m in alice_results)
>     assert all("Charlie grows tomatoes" not in m.content for m in alice_results)
> 
>     assert charlie_results == [] or all("Python" not in m.content for m in charlie_results)
> ```
> 
> ## What it validates
> - user scoping is enforced in retrieval
> - no cross-user memory contamination
> 
> ---
> 
> # Why these three first?
> 
> Because together they cover the three most important failure modes:
> 
> 1. **Within-conversation memory doesn’t actually help generation**
> 2. **Between-conversation memory doesn’t persist correctly**
> 3. **Multi-user isolation breaks**
> 
> That’s a very strong starting test suite.
> 
