> # `store_sqlalchemy.py`
> 
> Now the SQLAlchemy version.
> 
> This needs to do a few annoying things cleanly:
> 
> - store structured memory
> - store transcripts/messages
> - store user profiles
> - store tasks
> - encode list/dict fields as JSON
> - support multi-user isolation
> - remain simple enough for SQLite or Postgres
> 
> I recommend storing:
> - one row per conversation
> - one row per message
> - one row per memory
> - one row per user profile
> - one row per task
> 
> I’ll use JSON columns where convenient.
> 
