> ### B. optional `SelectorMemoryModel`
> A wrapper that delegates LLM calls to a selector-backed text-generation backend, if you want provider flexibility
> 
> ### C. batch ingestion helper
> Not as part of `MemoryModel` itself at first.
> 
> Why? Because batch processing is naturally suited to:
> - conversation summarization
> - candidate memory extraction
> - historical import
> 
> but **not** to live per-turn retrieval and state updates.
> 
> So I would not bake batching into the same methods that `ConversationMemory` calls during live prompt construction.
> 
> Instead:
> - `OpenAIMemoryModel` handles synchronous live operation
> - a separate batch helper processes old conversations offline
> 
> That’s the cleanest design.
