> 
> Good if you want minimal coupling to wrappers.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 2. For reliability-sensitive structured extraction
> A selector can be useful **if**:
> - Gemini sometimes gives invalid JSON
> - OpenAI sometimes gives invalid JSON
> - you actually track `success()` / `failure()` carefully
> 
> But I would **not start with the selector** for memory extraction unless you already trust it in production.
> 
> Why?
> Memory extraction needs:
> - consistency
> - low drift
> - parseable structured output
> 
> A single known-good provider is usually better first.
> 
> So my advice is:
> 
> ### Start with:
> - `ChatWrapBackend(chatwrap)` if it routes to OpenAI in a predictable way
> or
> - `DirectOpenAIBackend(...)`
> 
> ### Later, if desired:
> Create a `SelectorBackend` and use it only for:
> - `summarize_conversation`
> - maybe `extract_candidate_memories`
